{
  "schema": 1,
  "command": "ln",
  "help": "Usage: ln -s [-f|-i] [-r] [-n] [-T] [-b|--backup[=CONTROL]] [-S SUFFIX] TARGET... LINK_NAME\n       ln -s [-f|-i] [-r] [-n] [-b|--backup[=CONTROL]] [-S SUFFIX] -t DIRECTORY TARGET...\n{{help:help:0}}\n{{help:version:0}}\nThe last -f/--force or -i/--interactive selects overwrite behavior.\nDeclining an interactive overwrite returns status 1 without replacing the link.\nOrdinary option/operand errors exit 1; documented capability refusals retain their own status.\nOption values and operands after -- remain literal during alias normalization.\nNumbered backups advance after the highest valid positive decimal version.\nFailed backup recovery reports both errors and destination/backup paths.\n",
